    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nThis elegant four-bedroom Victorian terraced residence is a home of exceptional style, character, and charm, commanding spectacular coastal views in a truly enviable setting. Beautifully presented throughout, the property seamlessly blends an array of original period features—high ceilings, an elegant staircase, sash windows, reproduction fireplaces, ceiling roses, and ornate coving—with thoughtful modernisation, ensuring both comfort and integrity of design.\n\nThe versatile basement level provides superb additional living space, comprising a spacious fourth bedroom with ensuite, a guest W.C., and a bright open-plan kitchen, dining, and living area. Flooded with natural light, this inviting space opens directly onto a very private walled rear garden with direct pedestrian access to South Strand Beach. The garden is ideal for outdoor entertaining and relaxing summer evenings. A utility room and separate front access complete this level.\n\nAt ground floor level, a stunning dual-aspect reception room showcases the home's period elegance. A balcony accessed via a sash window offers breathtaking views across the garden to the sea. An office on the return provides an and inspiring workspace, perfectly positioned to take in the stunning views of the beach, sea, and the Skerries Islands.\n\nThe first-floor hosts three generously proportioned double bedrooms, including a fine primary bedroom with beautiful sea views. The remaining bedrooms are served by a well-appointed family bathroom and separate shower room, offering both comfort and practicality for modern family living.\n\nRarely does a home of such quality and character come to the market. Combining timeless period elegance with modern convenience, this exceptional property further benefits from privacy, direct beach access, and close proximity to Skerries town centre.\n\nWhether you're an avid sea sports enthusiast or simply someone who appreciates the stunning beauty and tranquility of the sea, this property offers the perfect combination of coastal living and convenient access to a wealth of amenities right at your doorstep. \n\nSkerries has been named Ireland's best town to live in - and it's easy to see why."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nBasement Level - \n\n\nPorch - 1.53m x 2.10m\nWith tiled flooring and hand painted walls.\n\nHallway - 11.11m x 2.10m\nAn impressive hallway with striking natural stone walls, recessed lighting, elegant coving and tiled flooring. A stunning contemporary staircase with glass paneling and glazed floor panels creates a wonderful architectural focal point.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.37m x 3.96m\nA spacious double bedroom with recessed lighting, decorative coving and an elegant open entrance to the en suite.\n\nEnsuite - 1.11m x 2.99m\nBeautifully finished with floor-to-ceiling tiling, recessed lighting, shower unit, WC and wash hand basin with built-in storage.\n\nKitchen - 4.05m x 4.27m\nAn exceptional open-plan kitchen finished with beautiful custom-made Canadian Red Oak flooring flowing throughout the kitchen, dining and living area. The spacious fitted kitchen features an abundance of wall and floor units, display cabinetry, a central island with sink and storage, built-in double oven, Aga cooker, marble splash back and luxurious marble countertops.\n\nLiving /Dining room - 4.95m x 6.30m\nDesigned with both comfort and entertaining in mind, the dining alcove features decorative coving and bespoke built-in seating for comfortable dining, overlooking the garden. The elegant living area is centered around a wall of bespoke fitted bookcases, while French doors open onto the stunning stone-walled rear garden with direct beach access.\n\nUtility Room - 1.28m x 3.30m\nFitted with additional wall and floor storage units providing excellent practicality.\n\nGround Floor - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 11.11m x 2.10m\nA bright and welcoming entrance hallway featuring recessed lighting, decorative coving, hand-painted walls and tiled flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 6.37m x 4.27m\nTwo magnificent formal reception rooms have been thoughtfully combined to create one elegant dual aspect living space. Features include timber flooring, recessed and feature lighting, ornate coving, a feature fireplace with open fire and views over the front garden.\n\nSitting Room - 4.63m x 4.27m\nEnjoying spectacular views across the rear garden and out to sea, this beautiful reception room features a matching fireplace with open fire and a sash window opening onto a decked terrace — the perfect setting to relax and take in the panoramic coastal scenery and island views.\n\nOffice - 2.85m x 2.33m\nAn ideal home office overlooking the gardens and sea beyond, complete with carpet flooring and decorative coving.\n\nFirst floor - \n\n\nLanding - 6.87m x 2.33m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.85m x 2.33m\nA luxurious bathroom featuring tiled flooring, recessed lighting, elegant wash hand basin and a stunning freestanding claw-foot copper bath perfectly positioned to enjoy the magnificent sea views.\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.34m x 3.31m\nA superb generous double bedroom enjoying panoramic sea views over the garden and coastline. Features include recessed lighting, decorative coving with gold detailing, carpet flooring, vanity area, extensive built-in slide robes and access to the en suite.\n\nEnsuite - 1.41m x 3.10m\nBeautifully appointed with tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, heated towel rail, wash hand basin with storage, bidet and WC.\n\nHot press - \n\n\nShower Room - \nFinished with tiled flooring and a tiled shower enclosure.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.83m x 3.19m\nA spacious double bedroom with carpet flooring, recessed lighting, decorative coving and built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.13m x 2.13m\nA beautifully presented bedroom with carpet flooring, recessed lighting, decorative coving, built-in wardrobes and vanity unit with drawers.\n\nOutside: - \nThe property is approached through elegant, gated pedestrian access with railed boundaries opening into a beautifully landscaped front garden featuring cobblelock pathways, mature planting and manicured hedging.To the rear, the property enjoys complete privacy together with direct access to South Beach and truly spectacular sea views. Enclosed by original stone walls, the garden features generous patio areas ideal for outdoor entertaining, mature planting, garden lawn and multiple seating areas designed to maximise the stunning coastal setting.\n\n"
      },
